<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!-- =====================================================================
     PRJEDU_oee - AyMON example: OEE of a production line, shift by shift,
     for an industrial engineering course.

     One engine, two documents, joined the way a machine and a plant's
     MES (manufacturing execution system) are - by a few counters on a
     fieldbus:

       LINE/S00  the MACHINE. It makes parts - product A or B, in lots -
                 and loses time the way machines do: breakdowns, jams,
                 running slow, a changeover between lots, material that
                 does not come, parts that come out bad. All it tells the
                 outside world is seven Modbus TCP holding registers on
                 127.0.0.1:1505: running or not, why not (if it knows),
                 two counters, the product.
       OEE/S00   the MES. It reads those registers twice a second and
                 turns them into time: planned, running, stopped - and
                 why. From that it computes OEE = availability x
                 performance x quality, live for the running shift and
                 once per shift into a database. The operator tells it
                 why the machine stopped when the machine does not know.

     A shift here lasts EIGHT MINUTES (SHIFT_S in db_OEE.xml), so a
     lesson sees several of them; everything else is in real seconds.

     Five connections and three documents: inside the FREE edition.

     Run:  run.bat,  then open  http://127.0.0.1:8100/
     ===================================================================== -->
<xdb id="XDB" xdb_lib="AyPRO, AyPRO_sqlite" xdb_log="4" log_cfg="0x39C0" log_lnk="%PRJ%/log/XDB.log"
     sta="0x0300" tid="S01">
	<config>
		<doc id="LINE/S00" sta="0x0300" src="%DB%/db_LINE.xml" desc="the machine - a line that makes parts, and its seven registers" />
		<doc id="OEE/S00"  sta="0x0300" src="%DB%/db_OEE.xml"  desc="the MES - time, losses, OEE, the shift report and the page" />
	</config>
	<data>
	</data>
</xdb>
